// Desert Treasure - the Bandit Camp (Corey, 2026-09-08).
//
// Three npcs moved out of content/scripts/_unpack/377/all.npc. Redeclaring a name that still exists
// there is a "Duplicate config found" build error, so the whole block comes with it; everything
// except the lines noted below is untouched cache data.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the shop
//
// dt_bandit_shopkeeper stands in the camp with op1=Talk-to and op3=Trade already authored and had
// no handler of any kind. The shop inventory he is meant to own also already exists - fd_bandit_bar
// in _unpack/727/all.inv, 40 slots, scope=shared, restock=yes, stocking bandit_brew - and was bound
// to nobody. Adding category=shop_keeper is what makes shop/scripts/shop.rs2's
// [opnpc3,_shop_keeper] fire; the shop params are modelled on Rasolo's, who is the nearest thing to
// a comparable one-line merchant in the cache.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the god-symbol bandits
//
// Both the Archaeologist's dialogue and the quest journal warn you not to walk into the camp
// wearing a god's symbol, and nothing enforced it. The mechanic turns out to be entirely
// pre-authored: the cache has three params - zamorakitem (88), guthixitem (89) and saradominitem
// (90) - already set on 36 objects, the hunt system reads exactly that shape via check_invparam
// (engine/src/engine/entity/Npc.ts:1039 calls player.invTotalParam), and _unpack/377/all.hunt even
// ships an [example3] doing check_invparam=worn,zamorakitem,>0 with nothing using it.
//
// A hunt can only carry one check_invparam, so the two fightable bandits take one god each -
// which matches the quest, where it is Saradomin and Zamorak items that get you attacked and
// Guthix ones that do not. Both types are placed several times around the camp, so wearing either
// kind gets you jumped. The sitting bandits are vislevel=hide scenery and are left alone.

[dt_bandit_shopkeeper]
name=Bandit shopkeeper
desc=I guess he sells what he steals...?
model1=idk_man_hair_medium
model2=idk_man_jaw_none
model3=obj_feud_desert_disguise_manwear2
model4=npc_1862i3
model5=npc_squirei2
model6=obj_priest_gown_manwear2
model7=obj_cert_drill_top_manwear3
model8=npc_1862i5
model9=obj_ikov_bootsoflightness_manwear
recol1s=14724
recol1d=32767
recol2s=2340
recol2d=32767
recol3s=7298
recol3d=32767
